{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>You shall not steal.</b> A warning against stealing money, but 'you shall not steal' in the Ten Commandments is a warning against kidnapping — a matter learned from its subject: something for which one is liable to the death penalty of the court." "<b>And you shall not deny.</b> Since it is stated (Leviticus 5): 'and denies it' — he repays principal and fifth, we have learned the punishment; the warning, from where? Scripture states: 'and you shall not deny.'" "<b>And you shall not lie.</b> Since it is stated (ibid.): 'and swears falsely' — he repays principal and fifth, we have learned the punishment; the warning, from where? Scripture states: 'and you shall not lie.'" "<b>You shall not steal, and you shall not deny, and you shall not lie, and you shall not swear.</b> If you stole, you will end up denying; you will end up lying; you will end up swearing falsely."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:07.483951091Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}